["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent co-worker, and product cycles last only three months OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent co-workers, and that builders must design for model capabilities two to three months out; the future of work is steering, not rowing, and the writing that is thinking should never be automated. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast AI’s third era: the rise of persistent AI coworkers | Tara Seshan (OpenAI’s product lead) Product cycles Persistent co-worker Codex Writing as thinking Product marketing fit persistent co-worker product marketing fit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-lennys-ai-第三纪元是持久协作者-产品周期只有三个月/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/67bb7dafb90c60da-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:21:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent co-worker, and product cycles last only three months</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent co-workers, and that builders must design for model capabilities two to three months out; the future of work is steering, not rowing, and the writing that is thinking should never be automated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Product cycles</span><span class=\"tag\">Persistent co-worker</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"AI Earnings Are a Bubble: Costs Deferred, Profits Front-Loaded AI infrastructure profits are realized now, while costs are amortized into the future, constituting an earnings bubble. The stock market will peak before earnings, so investors should be wary rather than chase. Excess Returns Excess Returns The Profits Come Now. The Costs Come Later. Kevin Muir on Whether AI Earnings Are the Bubble AI bubble earnings quality leveraged ETF gold trade policy Earnings bubble Leveraged ETF Off-the-run bond TGA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-excessreturns-ai-盈利是泡沫-成本后置-利润前置/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3cac5e72b6049e76-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:46</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Excess Returns</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>AI Earnings Are a Bubble: Costs Deferred, Profits Front-Loaded</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI infrastructure profits are realized now, while costs are amortized into the future, constituting an earnings bubble. The stock market will peak before earnings, so investors should be wary rather than chase.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI bubble</span><span class=\"tag\">earnings quality</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"1858 New York Poison Milk: Clear Evidence, Yet Officials Ruled It Harmless In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing ruled it harmless. The episode eventually led to the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class SYMHC Classics: Swill Milk food adulteration public health media investigation American history milk safety institutional corruption swill milk artificial feeding temperance movement spent grain\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-stuffmissed-1858年纽约毒奶-证据确凿-官方委员会判定无害/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcas