self-trained models—catching up from behind through iteration speed, hiring philosophy, and founder density. The a16z Show a16z Inside Cursor: The Anatomy of a Generational Startup Cursor AI coding startup strategy enterprise sales talent acquisition product philosophy self-serve back channel talent via acquisition monorepo\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-a16z-不做模型不早卖企业-用界面和速度赢下巨头/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7b2f032532c3a865-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">39:29</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The a16z Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>No Models, No Early Enterprise Sales: Winning Giants with Interface and Speed</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Cursor&#x27;s success is not about building its own model, but treating the product itself as a moat: no plugins, no early enterprise sales, no self-trained models—catching up from behind through iteration speed, hiring philosophy, and founder density.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Cursor</span><span class=\"tag\">AI coding</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Google Paid $10 Million for a Bankrupt Airline&#x27;s Data: Data Is the Moat in the AI Era In the AI era, a company&#x27;s most valuable asset is its data—Google paid $10 million for a bankrupt airline&#x27;s data; AI agents with legitimate access are the new biggest threat, and data infrastructure must be rebuilt. No Priors No Priors Rethinking Legacy Data Infrastructure with Eon Co-Founders Ofir Ehrlich and Gonen Stein Data Assets AI Security Enterprise Data AI Agents Cloud Migration NHI / Non-Human Identity PLG / Product-Led Growth Data Foundation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-nopriors-数据是-ai-时代唯一护城河-合法权限代理最危险/\">\n<div class=\"cover\">